Microsoft services failed for more than 12 hours, delaying hospital prescriptions and police work across Britain. This is Omni View, episode 235, Indonesia's vice presidential choice, Europe at the next Ukraine talks, and a tanker explosion in the Strait of Hormuz come in that order, then understanding the issue. Microsoft reported early signs of stabilization after teams, outlook, and other services failed for millions of users worldwide. The Guardian said, with no indication of a cyber attack.

